{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And make atonement for yourself and for the people.</b> This implies that the atonement of Aharon extends also to the people. The reason is that regarding Aharon's sin — Israel were the cause for him to sin, for they said to him (Exodus 32:1): ״קוּם עֲשֵׂה לָנוּ״ etc., and as long as Aharon had not obtained atonement, the sin still attaches both to its doer and to the one who occasioned it, but once he obtained atonement, both of them were atoned. Therefore He said to him: ״And make atonement for yourself and for the people.״"], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:54:34.339522965Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}